Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [product-specific log-level fix for BeagleBone Black Rev D Qt dashboard]

drm/bridge: it66121: use dev_err_probe() on the supply-enable path

The it66122 bridge sits on i2c0 together with the tps65217 PMIC that provides
its vcn33/vcn18 supplies (ldo2_reg/ldo3_reg). On a cold boot the bridge probes
before the tps65217 regulators are registered, so the bulk supply enable returns
-EPROBE_DEFER and the driver core retries the probe (which then succeeds). The
old dev_err() logged this expected deferral as a KERN_ERR on every boot:

    it66121 0-004c: Failed to enable power supplies

Switch to dev_err_probe() so the deferral is recorded in
/sys/kernel/debug/devices_deferred instead of spamming the console, while a
genuine non-deferred failure is still logged at error level. Probe behaviour is
unchanged.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c
@@ -1589,6 +1589,5 @@ static int it66121_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
-		dev_err(dev, "Failed to enable power supplies\n");
-		return ret;
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Failed to enable power supplies\n");
 	}
 	ret = it66121_get_optional_vrf12(dev);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
